# Potts, letter Fl - Fu

Flaccidly.; Flaccide. @AC 5356[end].

Flag.; Alga.

@AC 1691[5]. "The flags were bound to my head" (Jonah 2:5) ( = that false scientifics beset truth and good. @6726[end].) @AE 538[11].

@6726. "She set it in the flag by the bank of the river" (Exodus 2:3) = at first among false scientifics. "The flag" = scientifics... The reason "a flag" = what is scientific, is that in the Word every herb = some kind of what is scientific; a flag, which grows at the bank of a river, = a low Scientific; as in Isaiah 19:6... "The reed and the flag" = the lowest scientifics, which are sensuous. (Compare Sedge.)

@6732. "She saw the coffer in the midst of the flag" (Exodus 2:5) = the perception that truth was in a low state among a false Scientific.

