Fly.; Musca.

@AC 1594[4]. Occurs. @TCR 335[5].

@7441[2]. It is these (sensuous) falsities which are signified by "the flies of Egypt" (Isaiah 7:18). (See <Fly-Volare>.) @9331[4]. @10582[4]. @AE 410[6].

@TCR 68[2]. Than a fly against a camel.

@381. Like flies round the head of a running horse. @590. @ISB 14[6].

@SE 2922. [2921a]. They would all flee from a single fly. @3749.

@3332. I fixed my look on a fly...

@4304[end]. They are likened to flies...

@4743. Like the flies of a marsh which fly up in a body, and then settle in the marsh.

@DMin 4757. As easily as if they had been flies.

