@AC 2220[3]. That they were averse to the goods of charity, is signified by "fulness of bread" (Ezekiel 16:49).

@3254. "In a good old age, an old man and full" (Genesis 25:8). Explained.

@4620. "An old man and full of days" (Genesis 35:29) = what is new of life... (For) "full of days" = a full -plenus- state.

